<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{ appName }}&thinsp;&ndash;&thinsp;from Simon Tatham’s portable puzzle collection and more, with hints that explain</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Over fifty logic puzzles and games you can play in your web browser, for free, with hints that explain the next move.">
    <meta name="application-name" content="{{ appName }}">
  {{#if canonicalUrl}}
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonicalUrl }}">
  {{/if}}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/css/home.css">
    <script nomodule>{{{ noModuleHeadScript }}}</script>
    <script>{{{ colorSchemeInitScript }}}</script>
    <script type="module" crossorigin src="{{ preflightSrc }}"></script>
    <script type="module" src="/src/home-page.ts"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <home-screen>
      <header slot="header">
        <img class="logo" src="/favicon.svg" alt="" role="presentation">
        <div class="title">
          <h1 translate="no">{{ appName }}</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="subtitle">from Simon&nbsp;Tatham’s
          portable&nbsp;puzzle&nbsp;collection and&nbsp;more</div>
        <div class="controls">
          <a class="help-button" href="help/">
            <img src="/node_modules/lucide-static/icons/circle-question-mark.svg" alt="">Help</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section slot="intro">
        <p>Over fifty logic puzzles, free to play in your browser, with endless
          randomly generated games at several difficulty levels. Works with
          touch, mouse or keyboard, and <a href="help/install">offline</a>.</p>

        <p>Stuck? More than half of the puzzles can show you the next move
          <em>and explain why</em>. The rest are on their way.</p>

        <p>Looking for Sudoku? It’s <a href="solo">Solo</a> here, with
          <a href="solo?type=3x3xda">diagonal</a>,
          <a href="solo?type=9jda">jigsaw</a>,
          <a href="solo?type=3x3ka">killer</a> and
          <a href="solo?type=4x4db">mega</a> variants. Mathdoku is
          <a href="keen">Keen</a>, and <a href="towers">Towers</a> and
          <a href="unequal">Unequal</a> are close relatives.</p>
      </section>

      <noscript>
        <section class="warning">
          ⚠️ The puzzles are implemented in JavaScript.
          To play them, you will need to enable JavaScript in your browser.
        </section>
      </noscript>

      <footer slot="footer">
        <div>Credits, privacy info, copyright notices and licenses are in the
          <a href="{{ repoUrl }}">source code</a>
        </div>
        <div><small>In some countries, names of similar/related puzzles may be
          trademarks belonging to others. Use here does not imply affiliation
          or endorsement by their owners.</small></div>
      </footer>
    </home-screen>
    {{{ analytics_html }}}
  </body>
</html>
